    {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "case": "GUARD-CASE-11",
      "changed": "the design's 'frame restored' becomes 'the session ends': an abnormal guard exit reports guard-runtime with the engine's classification and charged work, the session is terminated and every later operation is refused; the exhaustion quota expires in the guard's reflection/type-observation work before its first execution step instead of inside dup/list.case",
      "reason": "The engine poisons itself on every abnormal guest exit and its worker exits, so no parked frame can be restored; restoring one would need the exact-release evidence decision 6 requires for live slots, and the Wasm instance state after a trap is not established. The engine charges guard and body work to one meter without marking where the body starts, so only a fault before the first execution step shows the body unstarted; caps of 2 to 32 already exhaust in execution work, where the body's start is not observable.",
      "decision": "OWNER DECISION 2026-11-22 (decision 33, delegated: 'do what is most correct/best long term'), refined by the integrator as decision 33a"
    }
  ],
